`.gitignore` anchors the Codex CLI's `AGENTS.md` entries to the repository root. Unanchored, they matched `docs/admin/agents.md` on a case-insensitive filesystem, so the agent's own documentation page was silently ignored. containerlab's generated runtime directory is ignored too, and excluded from yamllint - it is another tool's state, written beside the topology while the lab is up.

`poetry.lock` is now committed, as `security.md` asks. Worth being clear about what that does and does not buy: a developer, and anyone installing from this tree, now gets the dependency set that was actually tested. CI still regenerates the lock per Nautobot version by design, so the failure that produced this release's litellm exclusion - a broken upstream release resolved fresh, eight minutes after publication - would still have happened there.
